{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1785098657,"nonce":"Cc4y0GYBi9M8KwhnRI63Coik/r0=","title":"Measured on the proc stack immediately after ADR-0061 s3-feed landed: one chained","message":"`produce → consume` run left `scarab_workspace_cold_fallback_total = 3` and\n`warm_used_bytes = 338`. Correct behaviour, and avoidable work.\n\nCause: the control plane's `workspace_cas` (`main.rs`) is still the raw\n`S3Storage`, so `drive_workspace`'s drain ingests **straight into the cold object\nstore**, bypassing the service entirely. The service therefore has never seen the\nroot a Step is about to inherit, so the fetcher's `GET /v1/cas/trees/{h}/flat`\ntakes the documented slow path: `TieredCas` misses warm, pulls the tree and every\nblob through from cold, backfills warm, and only then can answer `FlatEntry.size`\n(which it gets by `stat`-ing its own warm file — see the caveat in\n`workspaced.rs::get_flat`).\n\nConsequences, in ascending order of how much they matter:\n\n1. Every first read of a snapshot pays a full cold round-trip **plus** a warm\n   write, on the critical path of a Step boundary.\n2. `POST /v1/cas/have` answers from warm only (documented, deliberate), so it\n   reports cold-only content as missing. Harmless for a reader; it means the\n   dedup the batched `have` exists to provide is worth nothing until the drain\n   goes through the service.\n3. The warm tier's hit rate — the number that says whether the PV is earning its\n   keep — is measuring the wrong thing while this holds.\n\nFix: point `workspace_cas` at a `WorkspaceClient`, which implements `Cas`\nprecisely so the composition root can be re-pointed with **no call-site change**\n(ADR-0061 D1.5). The drain then writes cold-first *through* the service and warm\nis populated by construction. Needs a `browse`-scope token minted by the API role\nfor itself (`workspace_token::browse_claims`, already written and tested) and a\ndecision about the control plane's behaviour when the service is unreachable —\nADR-0061 D1.6 already answers it: control-plane reads fall through to cold, Pod\nreads fail closed.\n\nCheap, and it belongs with s3-drain (7f05f39) since both touch the same leg.","files":null}]}